#################################################################
#  <scholar>  NO ADJUDICATOR ASSOCIATION IS PRESENT.
#
#  That absence is the whole point of this file.
#
#  Recording the model identity and version means that when a model is
#  later found to have a systematic error, every assertion it touched
#  can be located and re-reviewed. Without model provenance, a
#  discovered extraction bug is unrecoverable — you cannot find what
#  it touched.
#
#  When a scholar accepts this assertion, a second qualifiedAssociation
#  is appended with prov:hadRole mrs:role_adjudicator, the status moves
#  to mrs:as_accepted, and the record of who did it persists permanently.
#
#  That append is the moment a proposal becomes knowledge — and it is
#  the only way anything becomes knowledge in this system.
#################################################################


#################################################################
#  §9  PART OF THE HIJRA — a claim, not a plain triple
#
#  Slice 1b (maintainer decision 3, 15 Oct 2026) said these two
#  events are PARTS of the seed's Hijra event
#  (corpus/seed-incidents.ttl), not duplicates of it, and recorded
#  that as a bare crm:P9i_forms_part_of triple. Slice 1d (decision
#  O1) turned it into two Assertions so the link can be reviewed:
#  predicate mrs:rel_part_of (mapped to crm:P9i_forms_part_of in
#  relations.ttl), status PROPOSED, no adjudicator, no source
#  passage. The plain triples are gone.
#################################################################

